Android Progressive Concurrent Spectrogram View
Context
A custom Android View renders a live spectrogram timeline. Audio samples may be appended from any thread. The view analyzes complete sample windows on background threads, commits finished spectrogram columns on the main thread, and draws committed columns as a heatmap.
The hard part is concurrency correctness: analysis jobs may finish out of order, configuration may change while jobs are running, stale results must be rejected, zoomed-out rendering must preserve peaks, cache eviction must not corrupt visible output, and drawing/snapshotting must never deadlock.
Task
Implement ProgressiveSpectrogramView.
