Requirements
Use Android custom View, Canvas, Bitmap, Kotlin standard library, and JDK concurrency primitives only. Do not use Compose, TextureView, SurfaceView, RenderThread, coroutines, RxJava, or third-party rendering libraries.
The constructor must throw IllegalArgumentException if maxCachedColumns <= 0. Public methods may be called from any thread. Column commits and drawing must happen on the main thread, and View invalidation must be requested on the main thread.
Samples have absolute indices starting at 0 after construction or clear(). appendSamples appends all provided samples as one complete operation, copies the input array before returning, clamps values to [-1f, 1f], and treats NaN or infinite values as 0f.
setAnalysisConfig(windowSize, hopSize, bandCount) requires windowSize > 0, hopSize > 0, hopSize <= windowSize, bandCount > 0, and bandCount <= windowSize; otherwise throw IllegalArgumentException. Changing the config invalidates all pending and committed columns.
Column k analyzes samples [k * hopSize, k * hopSize + windowSize). For rendering, column k represents [k * hopSize, (k + 1) * hopSize). A column may be scheduled only after its full analysis window exists.
Band energy is deterministic: split the analysis window into bandCount contiguous ranges; each band energy is the maximum absolute sample value in its range.
setViewport(firstSampleIndex, samplesPerPixel) requires finite samplesPerPixel > 0; otherwise throw IllegalArgumentException. Pixel x represents [firstSampleIndex + x * samplesPerPixel, firstSampleIndex + (x + 1) * samplesPerPixel).
If a pixel intersects multiple committed columns, each band renders the maximum energy across those columns. Missing, pending, evicted, stale, or future ranges draw only the black background.
Energy is drawn as orange intensity: 0f is black and 1f is #FFFF9800. Band 0 is drawn at the bottom; bandCount - 1 is drawn at the top.
onDraw must never block waiting for analysis. It may schedule missing visible columns, but repeated draws must not schedule duplicate jobs for the same column and generation.
Analysis jobs must use immutable snapshots of sample data, config, and generation. A result may commit only if its generation, config, and column key are still current and pending.
clear() removes samples, pending columns, committed columns, and resets the next sample index to 0. Old worker completions must not repopulate the cache.
Committed columns are stored in an LRU cache capped by maxCachedColumns. Evict least-recently-used non-visible columns first. Columns visible in the current draw must not be evicted during that draw, even if the cache temporarily exceeds the limit.
renderSnapshot(width, height) requires positive dimensions, renders into a new Bitmap from one immutable snapshot of committed columns and viewport values, does not call View.draw, does not wait for workers or the main thread, and does not mutate view state.
debugState() returns a stable snapshot without mutating state, scheduling jobs, waiting for workers, or exposing mutable collections. commitThreadIds records the thread id used for each committed column since construction or the latest clear(); every value must equal mainThreadId.
The implementation must not deadlock under concurrent appendSamples, setViewport, setAnalysisConfig, clear, onDraw, renderSnapshot, and worker completions, and output must be deterministic enough for Robolectric bitmap tests and Roborazzi screenshots.
Tests
Invalid inputs
Verify invalid maxCachedColumns, invalid analysis config including bandCount > windowSize, invalid samplesPerPixel, and invalid snapshot sizes throw IllegalArgumentException.
Partial and complete windows
With windowSize = 4 and hopSize = 2, append 3 samples and verify no column. Append enough for 10 samples and verify only columns 0, 1, 2, and 3 are scheduled once each.
Out-of-order completion
Schedule columns 0, 1, 2 and complete them in order 2, 0, 1. Verify rendering is ordered by column index.
Clear rejects old workers
Start jobs, call clear(), complete old jobs, and verify no old columns commit and next appended samples start from index 0.
Config change rejects stale columns
Start jobs with one config, change config, complete old jobs, and verify old results do not commit.
Zoomed-out peak preservation
Place one high-energy column inside a pixel bucket with low-energy neighbors. Verify max aggregation keeps the spike visible.
Missing/future ranges draw background
Use a viewport spanning before sample 0 and beyond newest samples. Verify missing regions stay black.
Main-thread commit
Complete jobs from worker threads, run main-thread tasks, and verify every commitThreadIds entry equals mainThreadId.
LRU eviction
Use a small cache, render columns, pan so some become non-visible, render more columns, and verify least-recently-used non-visible columns are evicted before visible ones.
Visible protection
Set maxCachedColumns smaller than visible column count. Verify visible columns survive the current draw even if cache temporarily exceeds the limit.
renderSnapshot safety
Call renderSnapshot from the main thread under timeout while jobs are pending. Verify it returns without waiting and does not mutate debugState.
Snapshot consistency during viewport race
Run renderSnapshot while another thread changes viewport. Verify the result corresponds to either the old or new viewport, never mixed values.
Stress race
Randomly interleave append, viewport changes, config changes, clear, draw, snapshot, and out-of-order job completions. Verify no crashes, no deadlocks, no stale commits, and cache rules hold.
Roborazzi visual regression
Capture: before jobs complete, after partial commit, after all visible columns commit, and a zoomed-out spike case. Verify progressive fill, no stale artifacts, and spike preservation.

Reference Solution
import android.content.Context
import android.graphics.Bitmap
import android.graphics.Canvas
import android.graphics.Color
import android.graphics.Paint
import android.os.Handler
import android.os.Looper
import android.util.AttributeSet
import android.view.View
import java.util.LinkedHashMap
import java.util.concurrent.Executor
import java.util.concurrent.Executors
import kotlin.math.abs
import kotlin.math.ceil
import kotlin.math.floor
import kotlin.math.max
import kotlin.math.min
import kotlin.math.roundToInt

class ProgressiveSpectrogramView @JvmOverloads constructor(
    context: Context,
    attrs: AttributeSet? = null,
    defStyleAttr: Int = 0,
    private val analysisExecutor: Executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(2),
    private val maxCachedColumns: Int = 4096
) : View(context, attrs, defStyleAttr) {

    private val lock = Any()
    private val mainHandler = Handler(Looper.getMainLooper())
    private val mainThreadId = Looper.getMainLooper().thread.id

    private var generation: Long = 0L

    private var windowSize: Int = 512
    private var hopSize: Int = 256
    private var bandCount: Int = 32

    private var firstSampleIndex: Long = 0L
    private var samplesPerPixel: Float = 256f

    private var nextSampleIndex: Long = 0L
    private val samples = ArrayList<Float>()

    private val pending = LinkedHashSet<SpectrogramColumnKey>()
    private val committed = LinkedHashMap<SpectrogramColumnKey, CommittedColumn>()
    private val lru = LinkedHashMap<SpectrogramColumnKey, Long>()

    private var lruClock: Long = 0L
    private var currentVisibleKeys: Set<SpectrogramColumnKey> = emptySet()

    private val commitThreadIds = ArrayList<Long>()

    private val paint = Paint(Paint.ANTI_ALIAS_FLAG).apply {
        style = Paint.Style.FILL
    }

    init {
        require(maxCachedColumns > 0) {
            "maxCachedColumns must be positive"
        }
        setWillNotDraw(false)
    }

    fun appendSamples(samples: FloatArray) {
        if (samples.isEmpty()) return

        val copied = FloatArray(samples.size) { index ->
            sanitizeSample(samples[index])
        }

        synchronized(lock) {
            for (value in copied) {
                this.samples.add(value)
            }
            nextSampleIndex += copied.size.toLong()
        }

        safeInvalidate()
    }

    fun setViewport(firstSampleIndex: Long, samplesPerPixel: Float) {
        require(samplesPerPixel.isFinite() && samplesPerPixel > 0f) {
            "samplesPerPixel must be finite and > 0"
        }

        synchronized(lock) {
            this.firstSampleIndex = firstSampleIndex
            this.samplesPerPixel = samplesPerPixel
        }

        safeInvalidate()
    }

    fun setAnalysisConfig(windowSize: Int, hopSize: Int, bandCount: Int) {
        require(windowSize > 0) { "windowSize must be > 0" }
        require(hopSize > 0) { "hopSize must be > 0" }
        require(hopSize <= windowSize) { "hopSize must be <= windowSize" }
        require(bandCount > 0) { "bandCount must be > 0" }
        require(bandCount <= windowSize) { "bandCount must be <= windowSize" }

        synchronized(lock) {
            this.windowSize = windowSize
            this.hopSize = hopSize
            this.bandCount = bandCount

            generation++
            pending.clear()
            committed.clear()
            lru.clear()
            currentVisibleKeys = emptySet()
        }

        safeInvalidate()
    }

    fun clear() {
        synchronized(lock) {
            generation++
            samples.clear()
            nextSampleIndex = 0L
            pending.clear()
            committed.clear()
            lru.clear()
            currentVisibleKeys = emptySet()
            commitThreadIds.clear()
        }

        safeInvalidate()
    }

    fun renderSnapshot(width: Int, height: Int): Bitmap {
        require(width > 0) { "width must be > 0" }
        require(height > 0) { "height must be > 0" }

        val snapshot = synchronized(lock) {
            makeRenderSnapshotLocked(width, height)
        }

        val bitmap = Bitmap.createBitmap(width, height, Bitmap.Config.ARGB_8888)
        val canvas = Canvas(bitmap)
        renderSnapshotToCanvas(canvas, snapshot)
        return bitmap
    }

    fun debugState(): SpectrogramDebugState {
        return synchronized(lock) {
            SpectrogramDebugState(
                generation = generation,
                committedColumns = committed.keys.toSet(),
                pendingColumns = pending.toSet(),
                mainThreadId = mainThreadId,
                commitThreadIds = commitThreadIds.toList()
            )
        }
    }

    override fun onDraw(canvas: Canvas) {
        super.onDraw(canvas)

        val contentWidth = width - paddingLeft - paddingRight
        val contentHeight = height - paddingTop - paddingBottom

        if (contentWidth <= 0 || contentHeight <= 0) {
            return
        }

        val prepared = synchronized(lock) {
            prepareDrawLocked(contentWidth)
        }

        for (job in prepared.jobs) {
            analysisExecutor.execute {
                val energies = analyzeWindow(job.samples, job.bandCount)
                mainHandler.post {
                    commitJob(job, energies)
                }
            }
        }

        renderSnapshotToCanvas(canvas, prepared.snapshot)
    }

    private fun prepareDrawLocked(contentWidth: Int): PreparedDraw {
        val visible = visibleColumnKeysLocked(contentWidth)
        currentVisibleKeys = visible

        for (key in visible) {
            if (committed.containsKey(key)) {
                markUsedLocked(key)
            }
        }

        val jobs = ArrayList<AnalysisJob>()

        for (key in visible.sortedBy { it.columnIndex }) {
            if (committed.containsKey(key)) continue
            if (pending.contains(key)) continue

            val job = createJobForKeyLocked(key) ?: continue
            pending.add(key)
            jobs.add(job)
        }

        evictIfNeededLocked()

        return PreparedDraw(
            snapshot = makeRenderSnapshotLocked(width, height),
            jobs = jobs
        )
    }

    private fun visibleColumnKeysLocked(contentWidth: Int): Set<SpectrogramColumnKey> {
        if (contentWidth <= 0) return emptySet()

        val viewportStart = firstSampleIndex.toDouble()
        val viewportEnd = viewportStart + contentWidth.toDouble() * samplesPerPixel.toDouble()

        if (viewportEnd <= viewportStart) return emptySet()

        val firstColumn = max(
            0L,
            floor(viewportStart / hopSize.toDouble()).toLong() - 1L
        )

        val lastColumn = max(
            firstColumn,
            ceil(viewportEnd / hopSize.toDouble()).toLong() + 1L
        )

        val result = LinkedHashSet<SpectrogramColumnKey>()

        for (columnIndex in firstColumn..lastColumn) {
            val displayStart = columnIndex * hopSize.toLong()
            val displayEnd = displayStart + hopSize.toLong()
            val analysisEnd = displayStart + windowSize.toLong()

            val overlapsViewport =
                displayStart < viewportEnd && displayEnd > viewportStart

            val complete =
                analysisEnd <= nextSampleIndex

            if (overlapsViewport && complete) {
                result.add(SpectrogramColumnKey(columnIndex))
            }
        }

        return result
    }

    private fun createJobForKeyLocked(key: SpectrogramColumnKey): AnalysisJob? {
        val startIndex = key.columnIndex * hopSize.toLong()
        val endIndex = startIndex + windowSize.toLong()

        if (startIndex < 0L) return null
        if (endIndex > nextSampleIndex) return null
        if (endIndex > Int.MAX_VALUE) return null

        val start = startIndex.toInt()
        val end = endIndex.toInt()

        if (start < 0 || end > samples.size || start >= end) return null

        val window = FloatArray(windowSize)
        for (i in 0 until windowSize) {
            window[i] = samples[start + i]
        }

        return AnalysisJob(
            generation = generation,
            key = key,
            windowSize = windowSize,
            hopSize = hopSize,
            bandCount = bandCount,
            samples = window
        )
    }

    private fun commitJob(job: AnalysisJob, energies: FloatArray) {
        var shouldInvalidate = false

        synchronized(lock) {
            if (job.generation != generation) return
            if (job.windowSize != windowSize) return
            if (job.hopSize != hopSize) return
            if (job.bandCount != bandCount) return
            if (!pending.remove(job.key)) return

            committed[job.key] = CommittedColumn(
                key = job.key,
                windowSize = job.windowSize,
                hopSize = job.hopSize,
                bandCount = job.bandCount,
                energies = energies.copyOf()
            )

            markUsedLocked(job.key)
            commitThreadIds.add(Thread.currentThread().id)

            evictIfNeededLocked()
            shouldInvalidate = true
        }

        if (shouldInvalidate) {
            safeInvalidate()
        }
    }

    private fun evictIfNeededLocked() {
        while (committed.size > maxCachedColumns) {
            val candidates = committed.keys.filter { key ->
                key !in currentVisibleKeys
            }

            if (candidates.isEmpty()) {
                return
            }

            val victim = candidates.minByOrNull { key ->
                lru[key] ?: Long.MIN_VALUE
            } ?: return

            committed.remove(victim)
            lru.remove(victim)
            pending.remove(victim)
        }
    }

    private fun markUsedLocked(key: SpectrogramColumnKey) {
        lruClock++
        lru[key] = lruClock
    }

    private fun makeRenderSnapshotLocked(width: Int, height: Int): RenderSnapshot {
        return RenderSnapshot(
            width = width,
            height = height,
            paddingLeft = paddingLeft,
            paddingTop = paddingTop,
            paddingRight = paddingRight,
            paddingBottom = paddingBottom,
            firstSampleIndex = firstSampleIndex,
            samplesPerPixel = samplesPerPixel,
            bandCount = bandCount,
            columns = committed.values.map { it.copyForSnapshot() }
        )
    }

    private fun renderSnapshotToCanvas(canvas: Canvas, snapshot: RenderSnapshot) {
        val contentLeft = snapshot.paddingLeft
        val contentTop = snapshot.paddingTop
        val contentRight = snapshot.width - snapshot.paddingRight
        val contentBottom = snapshot.height - snapshot.paddingBottom

        val contentWidth = contentRight - contentLeft
        val contentHeight = contentBottom - contentTop

        paint.style = Paint.Style.FILL
        paint.color = Color.BLACK
        canvas.drawRect(
            0f,
            0f,
            snapshot.width.toFloat(),
            snapshot.height.toFloat(),
            paint
        )

        if (contentWidth <= 0 || contentHeight <= 0) return
        if (snapshot.bandCount <= 0) return

        canvas.save()
        canvas.clipRect(contentLeft, contentTop, contentRight, contentBottom)

        val bandHeight = contentHeight.toFloat() / snapshot.bandCount.toFloat()

        for (x in 0 until contentWidth) {
            val sampleStart =
                snapshot.firstSampleIndex.toDouble() +
                    x.toDouble() * snapshot.samplesPerPixel.toDouble()

            val sampleEnd =
                snapshot.firstSampleIndex.toDouble() +
                    (x + 1).toDouble() * snapshot.samplesPerPixel.toDouble()

            val maxBands = FloatArray(snapshot.bandCount) { 0f }
            var hasAnyColumn = false

            for (column in snapshot.columns) {
                val columnStart =
                    column.key.columnIndex * column.hopSize.toLong()

                val columnEnd =
                    columnStart + column.hopSize.toLong()

                val intersects =
                    columnStart < sampleEnd && columnEnd > sampleStart

                if (!intersects) continue

                hasAnyColumn = true

                val limit = min(snapshot.bandCount, column.energies.size)
                for (band in 0 until limit) {
                    maxBands[band] = max(maxBands[band], column.energies[band])
                }
            }

            if (!hasAnyColumn) continue

            val drawX0 = contentLeft + x.toFloat()
            val drawX1 = drawX0 + 1f

            for (band in 0 until snapshot.bandCount) {
                val energy = maxBands[band].coerceIn(0f, 1f)
                if (energy <= 0f) continue

                paint.color = energyColor(energy)

                val visualBandFromTop = snapshot.bandCount - 1 - band
                val top = contentTop + visualBandFromTop * bandHeight
                val bottom = contentTop + (visualBandFromTop + 1) * bandHeight

                canvas.drawRect(drawX0, top, drawX1, bottom, paint)
            }
        }

        canvas.restore()
    }

    private fun analyzeWindow(window: FloatArray, bandCount: Int): FloatArray {
        val result = FloatArray(bandCount)
        if (window.isEmpty()) return result

        for (band in 0 until bandCount) {
            val start = floor(
                band.toDouble() * window.size.toDouble() / bandCount.toDouble()
            ).toInt()

            val end = floor(
                (band + 1).toDouble() * window.size.toDouble() / bandCount.toDouble()
            ).toInt()

            var maxAbs = 0f

            for (i in start until end) {
                maxAbs = max(maxAbs, abs(window[i]))
            }

            result[band] = maxAbs.coerceIn(0f, 1f)
        }

        return result
    }

    private fun energyColor(energy: Float): Int {
        val e = energy.coerceIn(0f, 1f)
        val r = (255f * e).roundToInt().coerceIn(0, 255)
        val g = (152f * e).roundToInt().coerceIn(0, 255)
        return Color.argb(255, r, g, 0)
    }

    private fun sanitizeSample(value: Float): Float {
        return when {
            value.isNaN() -> 0f
            value.isInfinite() -> 0f
            value < -1f -> -1f
            value > 1f -> 1f
            else -> value
        }
    }

    private fun safeInvalidate() {
        if (Looper.myLooper() == Looper.getMainLooper()) {
            invalidate()
        } else {
            mainHandler.post {
                invalidate()
            }
        }
    }

    private data class PreparedDraw(
        val snapshot: RenderSnapshot,
        val jobs: List<AnalysisJob>
    )

    private data class AnalysisJob(
        val generation: Long,
        val key: SpectrogramColumnKey,
        val windowSize: Int,
        val hopSize: Int,
        val bandCount: Int,
        val samples: FloatArray
    )

    private data class CommittedColumn(
        val key: SpectrogramColumnKey,
        val windowSize: Int,
        val hopSize: Int,
        val bandCount: Int,
        val energies: FloatArray
    ) {
        fun copyForSnapshot(): SnapshotColumn {
            return SnapshotColumn(
                key = key,
                hopSize = hopSize,
                energies = energies.copyOf()
            )
        }
    }

    private data class SnapshotColumn(
        val key: SpectrogramColumnKey,
        val hopSize: Int,
        val energies: FloatArray
    )

    private data class RenderSnapshot(
        val width: Int,
        val height: Int,
        val paddingLeft: Int,
        val paddingTop: Int,
        val paddingRight: Int,
        val paddingBottom: Int,
        val firstSampleIndex: Long,
        val samplesPerPixel: Float,
        val bandCount: Int,
        val columns: List<SnapshotColumn>
    )
}

data class SpectrogramColumnKey(
    val columnIndex: Long
)

data class SpectrogramDebugState(
    val generation: Long,
    val committedColumns: Set<SpectrogramColumnKey>,
    val pendingColumns: Set<SpectrogramColumnKey>,
    val mainThreadId: Long,
    val commitThreadIds: List<Long>
)

